    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Sam Hill is delighted to present to the the market this gem of a mid terrace.No.14 is located just off the bustling Frances St and set back on a quiet street and built in 1918.\r\n\r\nAccommodation:\r\n\r\nDownstairs to the right is a large bright south facing living room which hosts an open fire giving the buyer another secondary heat source option. Just before you enter the kitchen on the right is an electric shower room.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen comes has a laid out open plan dining room with comes with wooden flooring. At the rear is the WC and right a small back yard.\r\n\r\nUpstairs:\r\n \r\nTo the rear of the house is a nice sized double bedroom and to the front is a large master bedroom.\r\n\r\nIn the master bedroom there is access to the loft which offers the future purchaser a potential Office space or storage options.\r\n\r\nHeating is gas and off St. parking is available.\r\n\r\nNo.14 is located just off Frances st.in the heart of the Liberties. Stephen's Green is a short walk away. It is a short walk to James hospital, National college of art and design and the Guinness brewery. Mollys bar( which is great for a pint and a burger!)and the Ginger cafe are located round the corner.\r\n\r\nThe area is served by the following Bus routes to city centre:\r\n\r\n150, 27, 56a, 74, 77a, 151, 13, 123, G1, G2, S2 and the Luas near Stephens green. St James primary school and CBS James St are nearby and there's a Lidl on Thomas St.\r\n\r\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***"
      },
